A||||28||BroCar 87||V8 project a go!!! got any tips/links for me???||||1||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||01-27-2001||09:31 PM||||For those of you that don't know, I am now going to be working on a project V8 fiero. I am wondering if you guys have any tips and/or links to help me through this?<BR>Here is the run-down...<BR>I plan on using the Archie kit, but want a performance shop down the road to do the installation. I have my eyes on a completely assembled 350 for carberated chevy vehicles up to 1985. It comes with the timing cover, valve covers, and oil pan too for $1290. Its a new GM Goodwrench350 Crate engine.<BR>The intake manifold and carb. are probably going to be Edelbrock as well as the air element. <BR>Do you guys/girls have any tips/links for me to find any cool or inexpensive performance parts?<BR>Thanks for ANY info.<BR>BroCar87||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||01-27-2001||09:46 PM||||Since you have to spend the base money($1290) anyway,how much more would it cost to get a real strong engine?All the parts needed will also be needed for any horsepower rated engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BroCar 87||01-28-2001||12:36 AM||||The main thing I am looking at in the engine department of my swap, is the price(and quality of course... I won't have any bone yard engine ruin my swap. I see 350's all the time for around 2000 and 3000 dollars, but I don't want to pay that much for JUST the engine! I realize that if I want MORE power than a regular 350 puts out in the long run, I should get a high HP rated engine, but just the stock 350 in my fiero would be an upgrade from my duke by far.||||reg||12
Z||000003||BroCar 87||01-28-2001||07:21 PM||||ANY tips or suggestions????? come on guys!<P>Ohh I was pricing carbs today, and got a little confused between electric and manual chokes. What is the difference? Any info on this would be great too!<P>BroCar 87||||reg||5
Z||000004||hugh||01-28-2001||07:47 PM||||Go with the electric choke,you don't want to mess around with a choke cable.Also don't go too big on the carb.A 600 CFMcarb will give you good throttle response.||||reg||1
Z||000005||v8vinnie||01-28-2001||08:31 PM||||yea i have a holley 1850 600 cfm, in my zz3 crate motor, but its old and when i go to change it im going to put a road deamon on it ,625 cfm, i had a edelbrock on my 67 vette 600 cfm and my gas mileage went up 2 miles pr gallon, but the carb would sometimes stall at parades when i would burn rubber for the by standers,i think the holley is better for cornering, but all carbs have their pros and cons, but believe it or nt the quarajet is the perfect all around carb once dialed in , thats just my opinion, buy any way i love TERRORIZING the rice crowd when the pull up beside me at a light with their 4 foot wings, some times i whish i could just rev the motor to 6500 rpm and the noise from my 345 hp v8 just shatter the wings off, YEA BABBY!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tina||01-28-2001||09:36 PM||||Since your your having the engine installed by the performance shop.<BR>I would start there.<BR>Tell them what you want, and what you can spent.<BR>The options here, are almost unlimited.<BR>I guess it just depends what your willing to spend and the size of your wallet.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> <BR>84 383SB<P>Pic's at <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||BroCar 87||01-28-2001||10:27 PM||||Thanks so far guys( and tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) I think I am going to try to keep the performance shop from gettin all my money, and do as much of the work as I can myself. So this brings me to my next question, Whats the difference between mechanical gauges and electrical gauges? Which ones do you prefer? I plan on getting a couple extra gauges in the cockpit of my fiero once the V8 is installed. <P>Hmmm, I know I will have more Q's, so I'll keep asking when they arise! haha<P>Thanks again<BR>BroCar 87||||reg||6
Z||000008||RobertVol||01-28-2001||10:44 PM||||Bro...<P>You really need to talk to Chris on this one. He is local and could help ya out with ideas. his e mail is around I will send it to you on private e mail.... <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||01-29-2001||10:15 AM||||The $1290 engine you mention I think is rated at 220HP. But they don't mention with wich intake manifold or carb. I guess that rating is mainly due to the cam and heads that come with it. Torque will be plenty and as you said, with what you have anything will be an improvement. I'm doing a lot of research now for my future project. Don't know if will go the crate route or the build myself. Please keep us updated on your progress.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BroCar 87||01-29-2001||12:22 PM||||Thanks for the HP reading on that engine Alex! Edelbrock uses the same engine for thier performer crate engine package. The only difference is that they use thier edelbrock heads that puts out 310 HP with 8.5:1 compression, and 320 HP with 9:1 compression. HEADS themselves, I see, Have alot to do with power too. ||||reg||6
Z||000011||BBBAD GT||01-29-2001||12:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RobertVol:<BR><B>Bro...<P>You really need to talk to Chris on this one. He is local and could help ya out with ideas. his e mail is around I will send it to you on private e mail.... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that, I have Chris' first creation (the V8 Fiero), and its a dandy.  He's a real nice guy too, would love to have him for a neighbor.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
