Z||000013||batboy||01-30-2001||05:10 PM||||Bro, thank you for confirming what I've been telling people for years. Stock Chevy small block heads are wimpy. Any money spent on head work is money well spent. Intake and exhaust goes hand and hand too. It's all about flow.<P>The place that usually gets most of my paycheck when I'm building a high performance engine is JEGS. My hands tremble and my eyes glaze over when I open up their catalog and see all those sexy hotrod parts!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jegs.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tina||01-30-2001||06:13 PM||||Bookmarked and catalog on his way   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||BroCar 87||01-30-2001||06:44 PM||||Well I just got off the phone with Chris, AWESOME GUY. He has an engine that he will sell me, it is capable off 375-400HP. It has bowtie heads, verry verry clean engine. He is going to help me when ever I need the help, ALSO JoeJoe is going to give me a hand with this project too. It looks like I am setting up a little team for this V8 swap huh!<BR>Batboy, I love drooling over those mags too! Summit is practically the same too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> love em both!!<BR> I will keep you guys/girls informed from here on... <P>Anyone got any performance prefrences that they like???<BR>Edelbrock seems to be the one to go with!<P>BroCar 87||||reg||6
Z||000016||batboy||01-30-2001||07:55 PM||||The tricky part of building a high performance 350 for a Fiero is the exhaust. It's a critical component that is not easily delt with. Slap the cast iron stock manifolds on and you leave potential ponies locked up inside. The only factory non-Vette manifold to consider is the Ram's Horns from the 60's to early 70's (especially trucks). The best of the Ram's Horns are a bigger diameter one used on Z-28s and maybe other hipo cars. Headers are the best, but I'm afraid there will be plenty of custom fitting and cussing to get it done. Paul has done a lot of research on this, so maybe he'll pitch in now.<P>For an intake, I'd go with a low profile (no room for tall ones unless you run a hood scoop) two-plane manifold like the Edelbrock Performer (not the RPM Performer). The Chevy HEI fits no problem, but I like the Mallory Unilite for a high performance motor.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Archie||01-30-2001||10:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by batboy:<BR><B>The tricky part of building a high performance 350 for a Fiero is the exhaust. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually the exhaust isn't that hard at all.<P>You have 2 easy choices.<P>1) The old style "Ram Horn" exhaust manifolds were used on various RWD Chevys from the late '50's thru the early '70's. The last of the manifolds was used on a production car in 1976 on the Chevy Pickup with the SBC engine.<BR>These manifolds can still be found in many a bone yard & are still being made NEW by GM. These units are very effective and are still in production because many of the Circle Track racers and Street Roddders still use them. There are 2 sizes of these manifolds still in production. If you decide to buy these new at your Chevy parts dept. Ask for the 1963 Vette Manifolds.... specify "non-Fuel Injection" for the 2" collectors and "Fuel Injection" for the larger collectors.<P>2)A company called Sanderson makes a header that is a perfect fit for this swap. It's their pn CC-90. Paul Herder originally turned me on to these a year or so ago. A picture of these headers on a SBC is below. Note these are not "Hug The Block" style headers, the term for these headers is "90 Deg. headers". "Hug The Block" style headers hug the block too tightly and cause many fitment problems.<P>Please note that, just like with any other application, Headers usually create a little more noise and underhood heat than the same application with Cast Manifolds would make.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Archie<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-313s_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||BroCar 87||01-30-2001||11:21 PM||||WOW  I love the looks of those headers, where can I research/buy them? Is there a website or catalog? Thanks<BR>BroCar 87<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000019||Archie||01-31-2001||10:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BroCar 87:<BR><B>WOW  I love the looks of those headers, where can I research/buy them? Is there a website or catalog? Thanks<BR>BroCar 87</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A person would normally look for the Sanderson Web Site or call them to order. BUT, if you call Sanderson you have to deal with a blond named Diane. Well let me tell you, Diane is a jerk, she is quite rude and couldn't care if you order or not. She is a part owner and not much chance of getting rid of her by complaining. Besides the factory direct prices are higher than you can buy them from the supplier I use. I order mine from <A HREF="http://www.centuryperformance.com/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centuryperformance.com/index.htm</A>  Search for CC90 .<P>Additionally, we also carry these units in stock.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000020||Tina||01-31-2001||06:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>   I order mine from <A HREF="http://www.centuryperformance.com/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centuryperformance.com/index.htm</A>  Search for CC90 .Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Better jet, call them.<BR>Had trouble finding them on the site.<BR>And triple check with the guy over the phone <BR>that they are in stock.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Just because he says they are, doesn't mean they really are in stock.<BR>Once you get them, check the welding job<BR>really carefully.<BR>The first set they sent me went right back to them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||CenturyPerfCEO||01-31-2001||07:41 PM||||Thanks for the links to our site (Archie and others). To save you the grief of the search page, simply click this link for the Sanderson #SDH-CC90 header for the SBC V8 Fiero conversion.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.centuryperformance.com/detail.asp?product_id=SDH-CC90" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centuryperformance.com/detail.asp?product_id=SDH-CC90</A> <P>Best Regards,<P>------------------<BR>Sam Solace - Pres/CEO<BR>Century Performance Center||||reg||2
Z||000022||KissMySSFiero||01-31-2001||09:58 PM||||hey Brocar...when do you think your goin to start?  william and i were gonna do a roof swap when he finds a suitable roof with a good sunroof.  doesn look like im gonna be doin any mods to my own car soon.  im puttin all my money into repairs and suspension fixes. ball joints and bushings and such.  but nothing cosmetic.  i also want to get some body work done.  any time your gettin ready to start email me and im there.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||14
Z||000023||Chris McDonald||02-01-2001||12:39 PM||||Bro-<P>I enjoyed talking to you on the phone the other night about the V8 swap.  I hope I did not scare you too bad about how much it is really going to cost and what kind of results you can expect.  <P>This could be a real win-win because I have to drum up some more $$$$$$ to build my big block.  I am sure you will be very happy with either one of the chevy engines I have.  The $2,000 aluminum head roller cam/roller rockers is the ultimate in driving excitement.  Since you are running an auto you should not have any clutch problems by exceeding 300hsp.  The other engine ($850) has a pair of sweet bow tie heads, trw forged pistons, cloyes double roller chain, and four bolt main.  It may even have a steel crank.  We will have to go back and check.  The bow tie motor will need a fresh set of gaskets, intake, carb, dist, and manifolds.  The roller motor with the aluminum heads only needs the intake, carb and dist.  I have a decent edelbrock intake and old holley carb that I might sell as well to get you going.  I have never been one to try and "profit" off of anything.  There is no doubt you could sell either one of the engines for the same or more if you decide to bail out on the V8 Fiero project.<P>Come on over and check them out.  <P><BR>Chris||||reg||14
Z||000024||BroCar 87||02-01-2001||02:03 PM||||Chris, I will give you a call today!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>I have found the perfect package for the intake manifold, carb., and cam and lifter package. Jegs has the Edelbrock Performer Plus Package. 600cfm electric choke carb, dual plane high rise performer intake manifold, and the performer plus cam/lifter set for $440. I have been looking around at some prices, and this seems to suit my interest the most. All edelbrock. I have noticed other places try selling the holly carb. with edelbrock intakes. I want to be consistant with my engine package.<BR>Thanks so far guys, but I have come up with another question....<BR>Which type of distributor should I go with. I know NOTHING about distributors, so if you could help me out on this too, it would be great! <BR>I see that Batboy suggests the HEI, or the Mallory Unilite, but I have no idea what they are...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>ANY HELP???<BR>BroCar 87||||reg||6
Z||000025||Chris McDonald||02-02-2001||10:12 AM||||Thanks so far guys, but I have come up with another question....<BR>Which type of distributor should I go with. BroCar 87[/B][/QUOTE]<P><BR>This is an easy question.  For a mild street engine a stock style HEI with vacuum advance will work great.  You can always upgrade them with better coils, counter weights etc.  You can buy them for around $99 plus core charge at the local Discount Stores. Just ask for a 1975 Corvette HEI distributor for a 350 engine.   There is a company called Cross Fire that I bought a "correct" cap from that fits the large body HEI and correctly routes the wires to the respective side of the engine.  It is worth the $44 plus shipping.<P>You have to be getting pretty serious about squeezing the last possible pony to step up to a complete aftermarket system.  Chances are you won't notice much difference on the street between a properly tuned HEI and full blown aftermarket system.  The race track and dyno are a different story.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Tina||02-02-2001||06:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>[dual plane high rise performer intake manifold, </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you check on your clearance, deck-lid wise?<P>Otherwise you might be in the market for a  scoop as well, to accomadate your carb and airfilter.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tina.gif">  <P>------------------<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||BroCar 87||02-03-2001||02:39 AM||||Well Tina, Its not actually a "high" rise... its the performer plus manifold from edelbrock. I am going to "hack" up my decklid for a scoop anyways! hehe.<P>Also people, I went to look at Chris' engine tonight. This thing was spotless on the inside. No wear at all on this engine, except the outside. Its exterior needs alittle help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  but its gonna be fun doing the work. <BR>Chris, I will call you sometime this coming up week about your engine. I SHOULD be getting my tax refund this week, this is how I plan on paying you. I will let you know as soon as I can.<BR>On a side note, I bought an engine stand today! Looks like I will have something to do this weekend... putting it together.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Well I will let you all know how everything goes with this swap as I progress.<BR>Thanks for EVERYONES input.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>BroCar 87||||reg||10
Z||000028||Chris McDonald||02-05-2001||08:48 AM||||Sounds good.  It was great to meet you in person.  <P>See you later.<P>Chris||||reg||1
